# Bench configuration for the manual tests. Copy to tests/.env and edit.
#
#   cd tests
#   uv run --env-file .env pytest manual/gpio_loopback/gpio_loopback.py -v -s
#
# Everything here has a default that works on the author's bench, so an unset
# variable is not an error - it just means "the author's board". .env itself is
# gitignored; this example file is the documentation.

# --- serial port --------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed where a port has to be named: the pytest sketch tests take --port,
# and the manual tools discover the probe by USB VID:PID + serial so they need
# nothing here. Uncomment and set if your setup needs it.
#
# If your host publishes stable per-device symlinks (a udev rule, or boards
# arriving over USBIP where the number is not fixed), point at one of those
# instead of the raw device - the number moves, the name does not.
# CH32_PORT=/dev/ttyACM0

# --- manual/gpio_loopback -----------------------------------------------------
# The two pads the jumper connects. Different ports, nothing else driving them,
# and never the SWD pads (PA13/PA14, or PC18/PC19 on X033/X035).
#   CH32X035 (LQFP48): PA0 / PB0
#   CH32V003 (TSSOP20): PA1 / PC0
# A plain pin number also works if the pad name is not one this parser knows.
CH32_LOOPBACK_OUT=PA0
CH32_LOOPBACK_IN=PB0
